  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "The sum of seven integers is \\(-1.\\) What is the maximum number of the seven integers that can be larger than \\(13?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "An integer larger than \\(13\\) must be at least \\(14\\). If all seven integers were larger than \\(13\\), their sum would be at least\n\\[\n7\\times14=98,\n\\]\nwhich cannot equal \\(-1\\). Thus at most six can be larger than \\(13\\).\n\nTo show that six are possible, choose six integers equal to \\(14\\) and the seventh equal to \\(-85\\). Repeated values are allowed, and\n\\[\n6\\times14+(-85)=84-85=-1.\n\\]\nExactly six of these integers exceed \\(13\\), so the maximum is \\(6\\), choice D.",
